<%# The page header (design system design.md, "Page header"; docs/design/design.md). Server-rendered
    rather than <rfg-page-header>, which draws its <h1> only once JavaScript runs, so the heading
    would appear late and push the page down. Same layout: the page's only <h1>, an optional
    subtitle, and actions at the right. Usage: render "shared/page_header", with title: and an
    optional subtitle:, and a block holding the actions. %>
<% actions = yield if block_given? %>
<header class="page-header <%= "page-header--with-subtitle" if local_assigns[:subtitle].present? %>">
  <div class="page-header-titles">
    <h1><%= title %></h1>
    <% if local_assigns[:subtitle].present? %><p><%= subtitle %></p><% end %>
  </div>
  <% if actions.present? %><div class="page-header-actions" data-page-header="actions"><%= actions %></div><% end %>
</header>
